.TH IMPROV-COSMIC 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-cosmic \- COSMIC desktop workspace for Improv models
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov\-cosmic\fR [model]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-cosmic
opens a model in a COSMIC desktop window (libcosmic): the desktop's theme,
light or dark, and its accent color; the XDG portals for opening, saving
and printing. The shown measure is a grid; category tiles above it, in
Rows, Columns and Pages strips, pivot it when dragged from strip to strip.
Typing on a cell edits it; the formula list under the grid edits a
formula, with errors located in its text. Every change is saved as it is
made. Without an argument the model is in memory only.
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
or a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fImodel\fR]
The model: a store file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME. Without it the model is in memory only
.SH KEYS
In the grid: arrows, Tab, PageUp and PageDown, Home and End (Ctrl: the
first or last cell) move; Shift extends a range; typing, Enter or F2 edits;
Delete clears. Ctrl+C copies the range (TSV, and an HTML table where the
clipboard takes formats); Ctrl+V pastes at the cursor; Ctrl+Z undoes,
Ctrl+Shift+Z or Ctrl+Y redoes. Escape closes an editor unsaved. In the
formula editor Tab or Enter takes the first completion.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICED_BACKEND
.B tiny-skia
for the software renderer (the default where there is no GPU backend,
as on illumos), or
.BR wgpu .
.TP
.B IMPROV_LOCALE
As for
.BR improv-gui (1).
.TP
.B IMPROV_COSMIC_SHOT
A
.I .png
path: capture the window there once the model has loaded, then quit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
improv-cosmic sample.db
improv-cosmic 'postgres://me@127.0.0.1/sales?sslmode=disable&model=plan'
.fi
